bibliograph-worker (0.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.4 release: OpenLibrary provider and admin contributor search.

    - Add an OpenLibrary provider (search, ISBN and OL key/edition lookups,
      edition and author parsing) behind the shared retry/breaker/metrics
      wrapper.
    - Make OpenLibrary the final hydration fallback, so the order is
      ISBNdb -> Google Books -> Goodreads -> OpenLibrary; an empty or failing
      provider still falls through, and the first error is rethrown only when
      every step is empty.
    - Accept `openlibrary` in the worker admin /provider-search endpoint,
      including ISBN and OL key queries, and add /contributor-search backed
      by OpenLibrary author documents.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:20:00 +0000

bibliograph-worker (0.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.3 release: contributor/publisher records and entity preparation.

    - Build and publish net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.contributor and
      .publisher records (strict YYYY-MM-DD dates, defs#identifier
      identifiers, optional image and blob), and dispatch pds_outbox rows
      by collection instead of assuming editions.
    - Mint contributor/publisher at-URIs at ingest and link edition snapshots
      to them through defs#contributor.ref / defs#publisher.ref.
    - Ship the additive, idempotent 0004-entity-records.sql schema: at_uri
      and metadata columns, partial unique URI indexes, identifier GIN
      indexes and snapshot triggers. It queues nothing on its own.
    - Add the idempotent entities.prepare task and `--prepare-entities` CLI
      to mint URIs, enqueue entity records and republish linked editions.
    - Scope the outbox backlog metrics to the published collection
      allowlist.

